from source presentation semantics. Generated vehicle masters were created with
Skeletal Mesh usage unset, so PIE could temporarily substitute the default
material while compiling the missing permutation. Vehicle master construction
now declares Skeletal Mesh usage explicitly. Exact master read-back requires
that target usage.

A bounded migration accepts only a clean generated master whose reviewed simple
lit or simple unlit recipe passes graph read-back. It changes only the Skeletal
Mesh usage flag and refreshes editor material state. It then verifies the
same recipe
and leaves saving to the caller.

The five master recipes currently used by Snake were migrated through that
boundary and survive a cold Editor reload with the usage flag enabled. A PIE
